# Source: Wikipedia summary
# Topic: Elements
T:Elements
T:Reference
T:Category
T:Science
T:------------
T:What it is
T:A chemical
T:element is a
T:species of
T:atom defined
T:by its
T:number of
T:protons. The
T:number of
T:protons is
T:called the
T:atomic
T:number of
T:that
T:element. For
T:example,
T:oxygen has
T:an atomic
T:number of 8:
T:each oxygen
T:atom has 8
T:protons in
T:its nucleus.
T:Atoms of the
T:same element
T:can have
T:different
T:numbers of
T:neutrons in
T:their
T:nuclei,
T:known as
T:isotopes of
T:the element.
T:Atoms of one
T:element can
T:be
T:transformed
T:into atoms
T:of a
T:different
T:element in
T:nuclear
T:reactions,
T:which change
T:an atom's
T:atomic
T:number.
T:Almost all
T:baryonic
T:matter in
T:the universe
T:is composed
T:of elements.
